ontrols the access  to the franchise can  our votes be counted  and what does that playbook do  to our democracy there are still forces  that are determined  to keep citizens from voting unless we  fight  for the right to vote our democracy is  put at risk  the fight over voting rights is  ultimately about power  the states have figured out how to stop  african americans  hispanics asian americans the young  and the poor from voting we've got a lot  of work to do we try to make history  the table bout to turn  the table bout to turn the table bout to  turn  yeah i've been flipping through my  timeline  trying to get my mind right my city  cried out  i've got to cool down but i'm under  pressure  now monet wrote turntables as our end  title song  taking the energy of the film and  her art her activism and pouring it  all into a song that's also  an anthem that speaks to change to the  table's surname  [Music]  i think it's a perfect alignment with  stacy's story where  the struggle is real and ongoing but  we're hopeful  but the song also doesn't sugarcoat the  struggle  she talks about raising her fist and and  the fight and the lies that americans  have been told  but it does give us hope  i will not concede because the erosion  of our democracy  is not right history is never a straight  line it's always a fight  we have taken people on this history we  have  ended on the hopeful note but now i  think  the lingering question is what do we do  it's about the right to vote there are a  lot of people who take it for granted  but then when they see that somebody's  trying to mess with them and take it  away from them it's going to make them  mad  and want to show up and i think that  that was also part of the  raison d'etre of the film  [Music]  the vote matters  you belong you have value  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

